Z||000000||grinthock||10-07-2001||09:00 PM||||After seeing a Cavalier Digital Dash in a fiero at the PA TECH DAY I want to do this!<P>Anyone else done it?  anyone HAVE one of these dash's they do'nt want?  I am looking for wiring diagrams and all the info<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||10-07-2001||09:25 PM||||Mom had a Cavalier with the digital dash, so I offer this little bit of advice:<BR>Don't do it! Those instruments were crap when they were new, and age has not helped them any. <BR>Her's had the dash replaced 2 or 3 times before it was finally retired.||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||10-07-2001||10:09 PM||||and I know many people who had cav's till they died with the dig dash!  I know of the issues...  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||10-09-2001||07:03 PM||||FWIW, my 1987 Cavalier Z-24 has 230,000 miles on it now, and the digital dash still works fine.  The original motor (a 2.8) was replaced with a 3.1, but as far as I know the dash is original.<P>Doesn't mean much, of course - just one datapoint.  And I tend to be lucky  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||10-10-2001||06:11 AM||||I bought a digidash out of an '87 Buick Regal Somerset last summer (or was it the summer before?).  I thought it would be pretty cool, but I couldn't find anyone who knew how to wire it up.  Since I'm not much of an electrical genius, I just let it go.  It'll go in a future project some day.||||reg||1
